      "preview": "בֹּ֫שֶׂם: substantivo masculino: especiaria, perfume, bálsamo, balsameira.",
      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">בֹּ֫שֶׂם</span></big>  <strong>substantivo masculino.</strong> <sup data-bdbh-source-label=\"1 K 10:10\">1Rs 10.10</sup> <strong>especiaria, bálsamo, balsameira (</strong>árabe <span dir=\"rtl\">بَشَامٌ</span>, aramaico <span dir=\"rtl\">בּוּסְמָא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܶܣܡܳܐ</span>, grego βάλσαμον; cf. Löw<sup>53</sup><strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 3:24\" href=\"/Isaiah.3.24\">Is 3.24</a> +, <span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּ֫שֶׂם</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:23\" href=\"/Exodus.30.23\">Êx 30.23</a> veja-se abaixo, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּשָׂמִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">Ct 5.1</a> (como se derivasse de <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּשָׂם</span>); plural <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּשָׂמִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 25:6\" href=\"/Exodus.25.6\">Êx 25.6</a> + 18 vezes, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּשָׂמָיו</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:16\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.16\">Ct 4.16</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>especiaria, perfume, odor suave</em> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 3:24\" href=\"/Isaiah.3.24\">Is 3.24</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">קִנְּמָן־בֶּשֶׂם</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:23\" href=\"/Exodus.30.23\">Êx 30.23</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> talvez assim vocalizado para distingui-lo de) <span dir=\"rtl\">קְנֵה־בֹשֶׂם</span> versículo <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:23\" href=\"/Exodus.30.23\">Êx 30.23</a>;—com isto cf. aramaico <span dir=\"rtl\">ܩܢܝܐ ܕܒܣܡܐ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">קני בוסמא</span>;—<em>especiarias</em> como dispendiosas, sinal de riqueza <a data-ref=\"II Kings 20:13\" href=\"/II_Kings.20.13\">2Rs 20.13</a> = <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 39:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.39.2\">Is 39.2</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 32:27\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.32.27\">2Cr 32.27</a>; presentes reais <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:2\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.2\">1Rs 10.2</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.10\">1Rs 10.10</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:25\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.25\">1Rs 10.25</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.1\">2Cr 9.1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:19\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.19\">2Cr 9.19</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:24\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.24\">2Cr 9.24</a>; cf. singular <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.10\">1Rs 10.10</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:9\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.9\">2Cr 9.9</a>; como artigo de comércio <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:22\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.22\">Ez 27.22</a>; queimadas no sepultamento <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 16:14\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.16.14\">2Cr 16.14</a>; designadas como ingrediente do óleo da unção <a data-ref=\"Exodus 25:6\" href=\"/Exodus.25.6\">Êx 25.6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:8\" href=\"/Exodus.35.8\">Êx 35.8</a> cf. versículo <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:28\" href=\"/Exodus.35.28\">Êx 35.28</a> (todos P), cf. <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:30\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.30\">1Cr 9.30</a> (palmireno, veja-se acima); armazenadas no templo <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:29\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.29\">1Cr 9.29</a>; empregadas na purificação das mulheres de Assuero <a data-ref=\"Esther 2:12\" href=\"/Esther.2.12\">Et 2.12</a>;<br><strong>2.</strong>  em outras passagens somente <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:10\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.10\">Ct 4.10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:14\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.14\">Ct 4.14</a> <em>especiarias</em>, versículo <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:16\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.16\">Ct 4.16</a> <em>seiva de bálsamo</em>, colhida <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">Ct 5.1</a>; <em>balsameira</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרֵי ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 8:14\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.8.14\">Ct 8.14</a>; <em>canteiros de bálsamo</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲרֻגוֹת בּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 6:2\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.6.2\">Ct 6.2</a>; cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲרוּגֵת בּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:13\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.13\">Ct 5.13</a> comparação das faces do amado.",
